# Next.js + Tailwind + shadcn/ui + Zod Figma Guidelines

## Tech Stack & Next.js Conventions

- Use **Next.js (App Router)** with **TypeScript** and **Tailwind CSS**.
- Default to **React Server Components (RSC)**. Only add `"use client"` when using React hooks, browser APIs, event handlers, or interactive forms.
- Use `next/image` for raster images and `next/link` for internal navigation.

## Component Structure & shadcn/ui

- **shadcn/ui Location:** All base UI primitives live in `app/_components/ui` (import via `@/app/_components/ui/...`).
- **Reuse First:** Always inspect `app/_components/ui` before writing raw HTML elements. Reuse existing `Button`, `Card`, `Input`, `Badge`, `Dialog`, `Select`, and `Form` components.
- **Installing Missing Primitives:** If a Figma design needs a shadcn primitive not yet in `app/_components/ui`, run or suggest `npx shadcn@latest add <component>`.
- **Feature Components:** Place custom section or feature components in `app/_components/` (or route-specific `_components/` folders), keeping `app/_components/ui` strictly for shadcn primitives.
- Use `lucide-react` for UI icons.

## Custom Colors & CSS Variables (`globals.css`)

- **Single Source of Truth:** Before writing color classes, always inspect `@app/globals.css` (or `@src/app/globals.css`) to check available CSS variables (`:root`, `.dark`, and `@theme inline` tokens).
- **No Hardcoded Colors:** Never use raw hex/RGB values (e.g., `#1E293B`, `bg-[#...]`) in `.tsx` files. Map Figma color tokens directly to the semantic utility classes backed by our `globals.css` variables (e.g., `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, or custom tokens defined in `@theme` / `tailwind.config`).
- **Adding New Brand Colors:** If a Figma frame introduces a new brand color not yet in `globals.css`, add the CSS variable under `:root` (and `.dark` if applicable) in `globals.css` and register it in `@theme inline` (Tailwind v4) or `tailwind.config.ts` (Tailwind v3) before using its utility class.

## Forms & Validation (Zod + React Hook Form)

- **Standard Form Stack:** Build all Figma forms, inputs, and modals with forms using `react-hook-form`, `@hookform/resolvers/zod`, and `zod`.
- **shadcn Form Wrapper:** Always wrap form fields using `Form`, `FormField`, `FormItem`, `FormLabel`, `FormControl`, and `FormMessage` from `@/app/_components/ui/form`.
- **Schema Co-location:** Define clear, strongly-typed `z.object({...})` schemas with descriptive validation messages, inferring TypeScript types via `z.infer<typeof formSchema>`. Place reusable schemas in `lib/validations/` or at the top of the feature form file.
- **Submit & Error States:** Style error states using semantic `text-destructive` / `border-destructive` tokens and disable submit buttons with loading indicators during async actions.

## Layout & Spacing

- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes and `className` prop merging.
- Convert Figma Auto Layout into Flexbox (`flex`, `flex-col`, `gap-*`) or CSS Grid (`grid`, `grid-cols-*`).
- Snap Figma pixel spacing to standard Tailwind scale classes (`p-4`, `gap-6`, `max-w-7xl`) instead of arbitrary values (`p-[17px]`), unless exact dimensions are required for brand assets.
- Build **mobile-first** responsive layouts (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`).

## Assets & Exports

- Save exported SVGs and images from Figma into `public/assets/` and reference them with root-relative paths (e.g., `/assets/logo.svg`).

## Screenshot-Only Conversions (No Figma Link)

- **Layout Breakdown First:** Before generating code, briefly outline the layout grid, flex directions, and component hierarchy inferred from the screenshot.
- **Color Approximation:** Match visual colors in the screenshot to the closest existing semantic token in `@app/globals.css` (`bg-primary`, `bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.). Never invent raw hex codes unless a brand color is completely missing.
- **Icons & Placeholders:** Replace any custom illustrations or logos visible in the screenshot with clean `lucide-react` icons or placeholder SVGs in `public/assets/`, and clearly note which assets need real files later.

# Recharts & Data Visualization Agent Rules

## 1. Check for Existing Graphs First (Mandatory Reuse)

- **Search before creating:** Before writing any new chart component or importing from `recharts`, you MUST search the codebase (`src/components/charts/` or across `*.tsx` files) for existing chart components (e.g., `ReusableChart`, `BaseChart`, or domain-specific chart wrappers).
- **Reuse existing wrappers:** If a generic or matching chart component already exists, import and reuse it by passing your dataset and configuration props (`data`, `dataKeyX`, `dataKeyY`, `type`, `color`).
- **Extend, don't duplicate:** Only create a new chart component if the required visualization type (e.g., Radar, Pie, Scatter) is completely unsupported by existing wrappers—and if you build a new one, build it as a reusable generic wrapper inside `src/components/charts/` rather than inline inside a page.

## 2. Component Architecture & Next.js SSG/SSR Safety

- **No direct Recharts imports in pages:** Never import `LineChart`, `BarChart`, `ResponsiveContainer`, etc., directly inside `app/**/page.tsx` or `pages/**/*.tsx`. All Recharts primitives must stay encapsulated inside reusable chart components.
- **Client-side boundary:** Every reusable chart component must include `'use client';` at the top of the file.
- **SSR/SSG hydration guard:** When consuming a chart component inside a Next.js page or server component, always load it with `next/dynamic(..., { ssr: false })` and provide a skeleton fallback so `ResponsiveContainer` never renders at `0x0` dimensions during static generation.

## 3. Data Passing & Performance Optimization

- **Strict TypeScript props:** Define explicit interfaces for incoming chart data (`Record<string, string | number>[]`) and axis keys. Never use `any`.
- **Memoization:** Wrap all reusable chart components in `React.memo` with a shallow prop comparison (`data`, `type`, `dataKeyX`, `dataKeyY`, `color`) so existing chart instances do not re-render when parent state changes.
- **Stable data references:** When passing static or derived data to a chart component, define the array outside the render cycle or wrap it in `useMemo` to preserve reference equality.
